    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c193e0f_9a10a966",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_sta_iface.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-13T22:51:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not fond of |ret1| and |ret2|. Both of the names are vague. And it\u0027s too easy to typo on for the other. Consider, e.g., |supported_features_result| and |capabilities_result|, instead.\n\nBut even better, consider using std::tie to capture the result:\n\n  wifi_error err;\n  uint32_t feature_set;\n  std::tie(err, feature_set) \u003d ...getSupportedFeatureSet();\n  if (err) {\n    ...\n  }",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "7c3468719049a7f4702e9258aeb588162824bf27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
